  "result": "I found the bug but haven't changed any code, because plan mode is on. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode to request approval, since that tool isn't available here. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/types.py:754`, `IntRange._clamp` returns `bound - dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the minimum (move up) and `dir=-1` for the maximum (move down), so for open bounds the result moves the wrong way:\n- With `min=0, min_open=True`, an input of `-5` clamps to `-1` instead of `1`.\n- With `max=10, max_open=True`, an input of `20` clamps to `11` instead of `9`.\n\n**Fix:** Change it to `bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add two cases to `tests/test_types.py`:\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"-1\"` should give `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"6\"` should give `4`.\n\nThen I'd run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-cheerful-blossom.md`.",
